course: dictionary
lesson: 8325
title: Rodent: the animals with growing teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rodent is a small animal with sharp front teeth that never stop growing. Read the clues around the word: «What makes a rodent is its teeth» tells you the key feature is the teeth, not the fur or the colour.
explain: The examples give more clues. «The harvest mouse is Britain's smallest rodent» shows that rodents can be very small, and «some glide between trees at night» shows that some live wild and come out at night. Many different animals are rodents, so the examples help you see the whole group.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Rodents have spread into almost every way of life» still makes sense if you think of small animals with growing front teeth spreading into every way of life. Animals with long pointed canines, such as cats, are not rodents.
fact: A rodent is a small mammal with sharp front teeth that keep growing.
fact: Rodents gnaw, so their teeth stay short.
fact: Mice, rats, squirrels, hamsters, guinea pigs and beavers are all rodents.
fact: There are over 2,000 kinds of rodent, from tiny mice to the capybara.
fact: Wild rats and mice can carry germs, so wash your hands after touching them and keep food covered.
exercise: «What makes a rodent is its teeth.» What is the key feature of a rodent? | Its colour | Its long pointed canines | *Front teeth that never stop growing | Its size
exercise: «The harvest mouse is Britain's smallest rodent.» Which animal is a rodent? | A cat | A bird with feathers | *A harvest mouse
exercise: Which of these is NOT a rodent? | Beaver | *Cat | Hamster | Squirrel
test: Why must you wash your hands after touching wild rats? | *Because wild rats and mice can carry germs | Because rodents' teeth are wet | Because rats are a kind of bird | Because they are very clean
test: «Lemmings are small tundra rodents whose numbers rise and fall hugely every few years.» What does this tell you about lemmings? | They live only in Antarctica | They have long pointed canines | They always jump off cliffs on purpose | *Their numbers change a lot over the years
exam: «There are over 2,000 kinds of rodent, living on every continent except Antarctica.» Where do rodents NOT live? | Europe | Asia | Africa | *Antarctica
